<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulpa</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>the fleshy portion of
				animal bodies</i>, <i>solid flesh</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">spiritus non inter nervos et pulpas, sed in
					visceribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 6, 24, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 83</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulpam voras,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 77, 6</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 117, 30</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulpa est caro sine pinguedine,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Isid. Orig. 11, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> (Cf. Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σάρξ</span>, of sensuality.) Scelerata, i. e.
				<i>corrupt human nature</i>, <i><span class="en">Pers. 2,
			62</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4,
			95</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Of persons: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plebeiam numeros docere pulpam,</span>”
				<i>common people</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 4, 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>The fleshy part</i>, <i>pulp</i> of
			fruit, <i><span class="en">Scrib. Larg. 74</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Pall. 4, 10 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>D.</b>
			<i>The pith</i> of wood, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				38, 73, § 184</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
